      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hi, I’m glad you came in. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S005",
      "patient_response": "Well, I'm here because... honestly, I just can't seem to keep my work in order anymore. I work at a dry cleaner's, and it's just getting to be too much. The tickets, the receipts, notes from the workshop, customer jobs—it all just gets piled together until I have absolutely no idea what to handle first. It's a mess. \n\nAnd you know, speaking of messes, my sister came over last weekend and she brought her new dog, a little terrier mix, and it just tore through my living room. I mean, pillows everywhere, knocked over a plant... I spent the whole Sunday just trying to get the dirt out of the rug. Have you ever tried to get potting soil out of a shag rug? It's impossible. I tried everything, even that foaming cleaner they show on TV, but it just made it worse. Anyway, what was I saying? Oh, right, work. Yeah, it's just... everything is just in piles at work and I don't know where to start.",
