      "doctor_question": "Do you spend a lot of your day worrying?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Worrying? No, not really. I mean, I wouldn't say I spend my day worrying. I just get overwhelmed with the piles, you know? But I don't sit around chewing my nails about what's going to happen tomorrow. \n\nActually, speaking of chewing nails, my sister used to do that when we were kids. She’d chew them right down to the quick. My mom tried everything to get her to stop. She even bought this special clear nail polish that tasted like hot peppers. It smelled awful, like... like old vinegar and jalapeños. I accidentally got some on my fingers once when I was helping her paint her nails, and I rubbed my eye later that day. Oh my gosh, it burned so bad! We had to flush my eye out in the kitchen sink for like ten minutes. And the worst part was, the water pressure in that old house was terrible. It was just a little trickle. My dad was always saying he was going to fix the pipes, but he spent all his time working on that old Chevy in the garage. He loved that car. It was this bright cherry red... wait, what was the question? Oh, worrying. No, I don't really worry much. Just... distracted, I guess.",
